From 62ede3a4914e3f02a8a1f3be67b6243975e34433 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:54:23 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] HTMLVideoElement: the user's choice of how a video
 holds its views

The video context menu gets a 3D Video submenu: Automatic, Not 3D, Side
by Side, Side by Side Right Eye First, Top and Bottom, Top and Bottom
Right Eye First. The choice is kept on the element (stereoChoice, for the
browser's own UI only; pages do not see it) and applied to each frame
the element shows that carries no mark of its own: it comes after the
stream's frame packing SEI and the container's mark, and before the
picture's shape. A paused video takes it with its next frame.

Frames decoded in the media process reach the page as references to the
decoded picture; the choice travels with their descriptor
(SurfaceDescriptorRemoteDecoder), and the compositor applies it to the
picture, again only when the picture has no mark of its own.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
